417] [17592186054009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186054013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186054014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054009 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054009 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054009 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186054014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054009 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5c9c30ac-745b-5ac6-8f1f-5c84b0f7083a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054010 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054010 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054010 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "96517480-c58a-580a-bd6c-7724f8c25364" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054011 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054011 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054011 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d6f3604e-93c4-543c-85d4-015c8fe7e1ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054012 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054012 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054012 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f2d3f4da-921c-581d-b2f2-9c94396b9176" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054013 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054013 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054013 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1bd17a35-4d96-574e-94c2-099f33db7738" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054014 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054014 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054014 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2d69af09-12b4-5f14-a76b-d95e41ad99a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054540 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4089" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054540 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\log_{16}(32)$ without using a calculator." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054540 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fc85eeb4-dbc0-5ea7-af3a-60270d6ae722" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054540 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n\\log_a X = \\dfrac {\\log_b X} {\\log_b a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=16$ and $X =32.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $2,$ we set $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{16}⁡(32) & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(32)}{{log}_{2}⁡(16)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{5})}{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054541 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4091" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054541 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\log x ?$ \n\nI. $\\dfrac {\\log_{2} x} {\\log_{2} 10}$\n\nII. $\\dfrac {\\log_{2} 10} {\\log_{2} x}$\n\nIII. $\\log_{2}\\left(\\dfrac{x}{10}\\right)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054541 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "15844e53-9573-5e6f-8fef-debbe0a142ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054541 #edb/ref 1074 "The change of base formula for logarithms is\n\n$$\n\\log_a X = \\dfrac {\\log_b X} {\\log_b a}.\n$$\n\nThe change of base formula works with any new base. In this example, the choices are written using base $2,$ so we rewrite $\\log x$ in terms of $\\log_2.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡x & ={log}_{10}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{{log}_{2}⁡10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054543 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4100" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054543 #edb/ref 1071 "Use a calculator to evaluate $\\log_3 (7)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054543 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "890afebc-d130-5dbc-aaf7-c2cd4db193f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054543 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's calculate $\\log_3 (7)$ by changing the base $3$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n\\log_a X = \\dfrac {\\log_b X} {\\log_b a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=3,$ $X =7,$ and $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{3}⁡(7) & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(7)}{{log}_{10}⁡(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{0.845\\,10}{0.477\\,12} \\\\  & ≈1.77.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054744 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054744 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054744 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054744 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054744 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054744 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054744 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186522741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054744 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186522747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054744 #edb/ref 1039 "Rewriting a Logarithm Using the Change of Base Formula" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054744 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054744 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "87ee4eae-702f-59f0-aff4-46c9acb89f6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186522725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186522812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1039 "Evaluating a Logarithm With a Calculator Using the Change of Base Formula" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054745 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bccd26ff-1dc5-5817-962b-a1ef1f46b2fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054746 #edb/ref 1039 "Evaluating a Logarithm Without a Calculator Using the Change of Base Formula" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054746 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054746 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "e0ab12b8-b1c9-5192-91be-cebc968d9587" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054890 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054890 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054890 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054890 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054890 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054890 #edb/ref 1045 "The Change of Base Formula for Logarithms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054890 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186055747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054890 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054890 #edb/ref 1050 540.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054890 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "bfe70dfc-da4d-55b4-a070-178f1424a5d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055183 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186052384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055183 #edb/ref 1069 "q-262884" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055183 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055183 #edb/ref 1071 "Expressed as a fraction in its simplest form, ${log}_{16}⁡(64)$ equals{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055183 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3ba35fd5-f0a2-573b-abd8-5bda612260aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055183 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=16$ and $X=64.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $2,$ we set $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{16}⁡(64) & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(64)}{{log}_{2}⁡(16)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{6})}{{log}_{2}⁡({2}^{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055462 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186054009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055462 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66882" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055462 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055462 #edb/ref 1071 "${log}_{36}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{6})=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055462 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d4f6e3a6-36a7-5dcc-b176-d20ea50c924d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055462 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=36$ and $X=\\sqrt[3]{6}.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ can be presented as a power of $6,$ we set $b=6.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{36}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{6}) & =\\frac{{log}_{6}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{6})}{{log}_{6}⁡(36)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{6}⁡({6}^{1/3})}{{log}_{6}⁡({6}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055747 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055747 #edb/ref 1061 467832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055747 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "59ad328c-2f78-5aea-b0d1-6ed4bc8f3800" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055747 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186055970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055748 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055748 #edb/ref 1061 467833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055748 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eb11f291-8fc6-5293-8cde-d3a6827123ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055748 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055749 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055749 #edb/ref 1061 467837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055749 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1afbdf86-d560-5101-b414-37b5d5f9909a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055749 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055750 #edb/ref 1061 467840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055750 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1a1e953e-dcb3-521f-91dc-5eadcdc1b57e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055750 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055970 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we wish to evaluate $\\log_{4}9,$ but our calculator only has a key for the common logarithm $\\log$ (base $10$).\n\nIn such cases, we can use the **change of base formula**, which states that\n\n$$\n\\log_a X = \\dfrac {\\log_b X} {\\log_b a}.\n$$\n\nIt effectively allows us to change a logarithm from one base, $a,$ to another, $b.$ Note that $X,$ $a,$ and $b$ have to be all greater than zero and that $a \\ne 1,$ $b \\ne 1.$ \n\nWe usually choose the value of base $b$ that makes the problem easier. In particular, if we need to evaluate the expression using a calculator, we choose $b=10$ or $b=e$. \n\nFor example, to evaluate $\\log_{4}9$ using this formula, we can rewrite the logarithm from base $a=4$ to base $b=10.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{4}⁡9 & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡9}{\\operatorname{log}⁡4} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{0.954\\,242}{0.602\\,059} \\\\  & =1.585\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055970 #edb/ref 1065 2797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055970 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "bb104b87-e850-5cff-9826-fdd61c0287d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055970 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522059 #edb/ref 1080 "0.812" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522059 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522059 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "13b65618-43ee-532e-a839-a31e265d785c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522070 #edb/ref 1080 "0.917" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522070 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522070 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "180aac80-cd6c-553f-9390-bd5447a64e03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522092 #edb/ref 1080 "0.714" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522092 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522092 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "202305ae-992e-5dff-bc4e-bc45335f1658" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522164 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522164 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522164 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "42c12419-a232-5cd2-b235-39a6a1843fb6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522241 #edb/ref 1080 "0.893" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522241 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522241 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6d30e107-e689-5ca8-ade5-ea5a816ad541" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522388 #edb/ref 1080 "0.765" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522388 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522388 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b3c52165-df02-5476-941b-b3846aa44552" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522440 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522440 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522440 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ca66def7-3c65-5210-99d9-f0db68c4888c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522509 #edb/ref 1080 "1.416" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522509 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522509 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e53d2060-f4c9-588d-b716-6b6725d895f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522531 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{t}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522531 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522531 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f05b9105-6358-56c2-af8c-ebeaec8564d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522633 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522633 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522633 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522633 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186522509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522633 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "99060676-2b65-517f-864d-a46840395897" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522653 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522653 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522653 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522653 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186522164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522653 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cc3e8381-6b4f-5e93-ae04-8cf9545b1218" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522667 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522667 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522667 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522667 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522667 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522667 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522667 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522667 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186522059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522667 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e017985b-c529-50e2-9421-397fcbb26ef9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522672 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522672 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522672 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522672 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186522531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522672 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e5c30e83-ea24-50fa-94a2-e0cd96a4bf88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522725 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522725 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522725 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522725 #edb/ref 1071 "Use a calculator to evaluate ${log}_{11}⁡(7)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522725 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4c277570-c608-5c8a-9eec-65493369dacb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522725 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's calculate ${log}_{11}⁡(7)$ by changing the base $11$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=11,$ $X=7,$ $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{11}⁡(7) & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(7)}{{log}_{10}⁡(11)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{0.845\\,098}{1.041\\,393} \\\\  & ≈0.812\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522741 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522741 #edb/ref 1069 "q-262939" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522741 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522741 #edb/ref 1071 "If ${log}_{125}⁡x=\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{k},$ where $k$ is an integer, then $k=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522741 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7501f09d-5828-597b-9243-c1ed53d4a63e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522741 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nWe want to change from base $a=125$ to base $b=5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{125}⁡x & =\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{{log}_{5}⁡125}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the expression in the denominator using exponents, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{{log}_{5}⁡125} & =\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{{log}_{5}⁡({5}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{log}_{125}⁡x=\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, $k=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522747 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522747 #edb/ref 1069 "q-262839" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522747 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522747 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $\\operatorname{log}⁡x=t.$ Express ${log}_{1000}⁡x$ via the variable $t.$\n\n${log}_{1000}⁡x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522747 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "834c413e-3660-5a12-aa09-b30d7cd9a51f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522747 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nWe want to change from base $a=1000$ to base $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{1000}⁡x & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡x}{{log}_{10}⁡(1000)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the expression in the denominator using exponents, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡x}{{log}_{10}⁡(1000)} & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡x}{{log}_{10}⁡({10}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡x}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{log}⁡x=t,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n{log}_{1000}⁡x=\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡x}{3}=\\frac{t}{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522812 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522812 #edb/ref 1069 "q-262883" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522812 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522812 #edb/ref 1071 "Use a calculator to evaluate ${log}_{8}⁡(19)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n${log}_{8}⁡(19)≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522812 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd36bb1c-2d38-5fe5-b95b-ae2bbaecd296" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522812 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's calculate ${log}_{8}⁡(19)$ by changing the base $8$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=8,$ $X=19,$ $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{8}⁡(19) & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(19)}{{log}_{10}⁡(8)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(19)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(8)} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{1.278\\,754}{0.903\\,090} \\\\  & ≈1.416\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
